sequenceDiagram
  participant S as Signal or deadline
  participant R as Ravel CLI
  participant H as Harness run group
  participant W as Rhai worker
  S->>R: INT, TERM, HUP or the end of the deadline
  R->>R: record the first cause — a later cause does not repeat the stop
  alt a read is in progress
    R->>R: abandon the read — its thread may stay until the CLI exits
  else a harness run is in progress, such as an LLM call
    R->>H: stop request: TERM
    H-->>R: exit, or the kill-grace ends
    R->>H: KILL the survivors in the group
    R->>R: reap the child, check that the group is gone
    Note over H: a model service may still finish work that it accepted
    Note over R: a group that survives, or a reap that fails, is harness_cleanup_failed — it replaces the deadline
  end
  R->>W: TERM, and KILL after one second if the worker is still there
  R->>R: reap the worker, remove the private directories and report every failure
  R->>R: read the cancellation latch again — a consumed signal wins over the deadline and over a cleanup failure
  R-->>S: refuse with 128 plus the signal and raise it again, or else with 124, or with 5 for a cleanup failure
